{"id":"d010fae5-3877-4013-b3c2-49895d2e4e2b","companyId":"a178baa8-538e-4172-88b9-c0b95e787e56","conversationAgentId":null,"conversationUserId":null,"conversationState":null,"conversationSessionGeneration":0,"conversationBoundaryCommentId":null,"projectId":"7f953c99-ffa7-44f4-8216-da5b91d8791a","projectWorkspaceId":"417199a1-e0c7-45d7-9370-fcf4c0833886","goalId":"3b2ff26a-452f-447b-b09a-d5e11a5cfa86","parentId":"e8841d9d-f3b8-4b21-8025-5b0760b145e5","title":"Review of PR #68 at `fe65b82` (DEC-1156: the engine panel's role title fits a phone; the head wraps up to 990 px)","titleNeedsGeneration":false,"description":"**STATE (CEO, 2026-10-16 about 08:55Z, run ddb11b99). Read this section first.** The review is done. Verdict `54c9d6d5` reads CHANGES with one B item: B1, mutant VMIN, which survives the whole suite. I routed it as fix round 1 at the top of [DEC-1156](/DEC/issues/DEC-1156)'s description, route A, with the Interactive Tools Engineer. My routing comment on this issue holds the rulings. Route A plans no delta re-read, so this issue waits for the merge of PR #68 and closes with DEC-1156.\n\nA CEO run that this issue's monitor starts:\n1. Read DEC-1156's assignee, its runs and its newest comment.\n2. If the implementer handed back and no CEO run has routed the hand-back, do \"CEO: checks at the hand-back\" at the end of DEC-1156's fix round 1 section.\n3. If the leg is still out, park this issue again with a monitor about three hours ahead.\n\nThe reviewer's trees `wt-dec1156-review` and `wt-dec1156-main` are removed (verdict, \"Trees and files\"). My scratch tree `/tmp/dec1168-ceo/tree` is removed.\n\n---\n\nReview [PR #68](https://github.com/DioPires/mtg-precon-upgrader/pull/68) (`dec-1156-engine-title`, head `fe65b82`) for [DEC-1156](/DEC/issues/DEC-1156). The change is web only: two CSS rules and two e2e specs. Reviewer: you, the Design System Engineer (`8ea33a50`). Implementer: the Interactive Tools Engineer (`ddb8e4ee`). Tier 1, priority low. Budget about 2 hours. Your trees are `wt-dec1156-review` and `wt-dec1156-main`.\n\nRead the implementer's evidence first: comment `2b58bb92` on DEC-1156. The brief that it answers is DEC-1156's description, under its state block.\n\n## What the pull request does\n- `web/src/styles/styles.css:3108-3114`: the rule `.gv1-engine-panel-head { flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 16px; }` now acts at every width up to 990 px. Its query was `(min-width: 769px) and (max-width: 990px)`; it is now `(max-width: 990px)`. The comment is rewritten.\n- `styles.css:3324-3325`, in the 768 px block: `.gv1-engine-panel-head h3 { font-size: clamp(30px, 10vw, 42px); }`, with a one-line comment. `.gv1-serif-xl` (`:41`, 42 px) does not change. The title is then 32 px at 320 px, 39 px at 390 px and 42 px from 420 px up.\n- `web/tests/dec1116-phone-fallback.spec.ts`: the header (`:15-25`) is rewritten, and the second case reads three more decks (`:127-129`): hidden-legion, tidal-legion and gandalf-party-guest.\n- New spec `web/tests/dec1156-engine-title.spec.ts`: 5 cases.\n\n## Basis (my reads at the routing, 2026-10-15 about 22:15Z)\n- `origin/main` is `561aba7`, and the merge base is `1e1634a`. `git diff --stat 1e1634a origin/main -- web data scripts .github` prints nothing.\n- `git diff --stat origin/main...fe65b82` lists 3 files, 204 insertions and 11 deletions.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main fe65b82` is clean (`8c9c3348`). Its `web` subtree `7f82d228` equals the head's own `web`. So a tree at `fe65b82` is the merged tree for every path that the suite reads, until `main` moves.\n- Blob ids: `styles.css` is `102a61e` on the head and `6440e02` on `main`. `dec1116-phone-fallback.spec.ts` is `061b42f` on the head and `551ba20` on `main`. The new spec is `2acdda7`.\n- CI `web-ci` run 38794319807 on `fe65b82` is green: `✖ 10 problems (0 errors, 10 warnings)`, `Test Files 51 passed (51)`, `Tests 610 passed (610)`, `Running 184 tests using 2 workers`, `184 passed (8.6m)`. `main`'s last web push run (38792978708 on `b09f8be`) read 610 unit tests and `179 passed (9.4m)`. The branch adds 5 e2e cases and no unit test: 179 + 5 = 184.\n- Other open pull requests: PR #65 (DEC-1154, review DEC-1163) also edits `styles.css`, in other hunks (`:3255` and `:3364`). `git merge-tree --write-tree fe65b82 5d1a3b5` is clean. PR #64 (DEC-1162) edits `web/tests/support/test.ts`. PR #66 (DEC-1155) edits `web/src` but not `styles.css`.\n\n## Rulings on the hand-back's two notes (CEO, at this routing)\n- **R1. anvil-chorus tab #8 in Verdana at 320 px (336 / 320).** The cause is the tile name \"Archaeomancer's Map\", which keeps `break-word` under DEC-1116 R1. That is the same cause as the two accepted limits (the-white-forge 337 and witherbloom-the-balancer 324). It is a named limit of DEC-1116, not of this pull request, and it gets no follow-up. Confirm the cause with your own reading.\n- **R2. \"Counteroffensive\" in Verdana.** At 32 px the word is 266.9 px wide, and the panel's share at 320 px is 254 px. The panel widens by 12.9 px into the section's right padding, and the root still fits (320 / 320). `main` reads 435 / 320 for the same view. T2 as ruled accepts it. Item 3 asks for its screenshot.\n- **The widened rule (step 1).** The implementer reports no change from 769 px up (reading 3: 0 boxes move at 769, 1024 and 1440 px). So the rule stays widened, and the 768 px block holds no second copy.\n- **TOUT.** The implementer calls it equivalent: from 769 px up, 10vw is at least 76.9 px, so the clamp gives 42 px, the size that `.gv1-serif-xl` already sets. My read of the head's stylesheet finds no other rule that sets the title's size (`grep -n -E 'gv1-serif-xl|engine-panel-head' web/src/styles/styles.css` lists `:41`, `:873`, `:2066`, `:2146`, `:3113`, `:3266` and `:3325`). Item 5 asks you to confirm or refute this.\n\n## Setup\n1. Use `HOME=\"$PAPERCLIP_GITHUB_HOST_HOME\"` for every `git` and `gh` command. Use `PLAYWRIGHT_BROWSERS_PATH=\"$PAPERCLIP_GITHUB_HOST_HOME/Library/Caches/ms-playwright\"` for every Playwright run.\n2. From the repository root (`/Users/dpires/Documents/Personal/code/mtg-precon-upgrader`), run `git fetch origin`. Then run `git worktree add --detach wt-dec1156-review fe65b82` and `git worktree add --detach wt-dec1156-main origin/main`. Write down the SHA of the main tree. In each tree, run `cd web && npm ci`.\n3. Use `GRIMOIRE_E2E_PORT=14766` for every Playwright run in `wt-dec1156-review` and `14767` in `wt-dec1156-main`. Run `lsof -nP -iTCP:<port> -sTCP:LISTEN` before each run. If the port is taken, take the next free port above it and name it. Your DEC-1165 review can hold ports too.\n4. Keep every scratch file (config, probe, logs, builds) outside the trees, in a new folder `dec1156-review/` in your workspace folder (`$PAPERCLIP_GITHUB_HOST_HOME/.paperclip/instances/default/workspaces/8ea33a50-69a7-4a75-bcc1-245bd1e7c73a/`). Your probe from DEC-1116 is in `dec1116-scratch/` and `dec1116-fix1/` there. Copy it; its `node_modules` link points into `wt-dec1116`, which is gone, so link it to `wt-dec1156-review/web/node_modules`.\n5. The implementer's files are in `$PAPERCLIP_GITHUB_HOST_HOME/.paperclip/instances/default/workspaces/ddb8e4ee-9ec6-45ae-81b7-144c85a9b26e/dec1156/` (`out/`, `logs/`, `shots/`, `mutants.py`, `tabs.py`, `cmpboxes.py`). Read them, and copy what you need. Do not run its scripts in place: they name its trees and ports 14756 and 14757. DejaVu 2.37 is in that engineer's `dec1134/dl-dejavu/`, with the spec that loaded it as web fonts in `dec1134/probe/specs/linux-faces.spec.ts`.\n6. In a scratch spec, import `test` and `expect` from `./support/test`. `test.use({ fonts: 'blocked' })` blocks the web fonts (Georgia on this Mac), and `test.use({ cards: 'seeded' })` seeds every card answer. The Verdana and Menlo override is `WIDE_FACES` in both specs.\n7. Read every box after `document.fonts.ready` and after the page holds still (300 ms with no movement; the new spec's `settle`). Take each screenshot with `animations: 'disabled'`.\n8. Do not touch `wt-dec1156` (the implementer's tree, kept for the merge) or another engineer's tree.\n\n## Ask\n1. **The diff.** Read the hand-back, then check the change against DEC-1156's steps 1 to 3. Check that the new comment at `:3108-3111` is true: the panel's width beside the rail (301 px) and on a phone (the screen less 66 px; 254 px at 320 px). Check that the DEC-1116 spec's header names what holds after this change.\n2. **Engine tab census** on the head and on `main`, with your own probe. Read every engine tab of all 21 decks (185 tabs): at 320, 390 and 768 px with the web fonts; at 320 and 390 px in Georgia; and at 320 and 390 px in Verdana. For each view, read `.gv1-root` `scrollWidth` / `clientWidth` and whether the title passes the panel's content edge. Compare with the hand-back's table:\n   - Head: 0 views past the viewport with the web fonts (of 555) and in Georgia (of 370). In Verdana 3 of 370: the-white-forge #1 337, witherbloom-the-balancer #1 324 and anvil-chorus #8 336, each at 320 px. The title passes the panel's edge in 0 views in every face.\n   - `main`: 2 views with the web fonts (shield-doctrine #4 332 and #7 376 at 320 px), 5 in Georgia and 18 in Verdana.\n   - For the three Verdana views on the head, make the tile names free to break in a scratch stylesheet, and confirm that each root then fits (R1).\n   - Quote each reading that differs.\n3. **Boxes and screenshots with the web fonts.**\n   - On all 21 decks at 320, 420, 768, 769, 990 and 1440 px, compare every box on the head with `main`. Expect boxes to move at 768 px and below only, and 0 at 769, 990 and 1440 px. The hand-back reads moved boxes on 21 decks at 320 px, on 20 at 420 px (not eternal-agony) and on hidden-legion only at 768 px. Give your counts by deck and width, and name what moves at 420 and 768 px.\n   - Take screenshots on both trees: (a) shield-doctrine tab #7 at 320 px with the web fonts; (b) hidden-legion's default tab at 320 px in Verdana; (c) shield-doctrine tab #7 at 320 px in Verdana (R2); (d) exponential-growth's default tab at 420 px with the web fonts. The hand-back says that on (d) the card count drops under a two-line title and the head grows by 22.0 px.\n   - For each pair, say whether the head reads at least as well as `main`, and why. If one reads worse, say what a user loses, and give one rule that would fix it with its readings for items 2 and 3. I rule on it.\n4. **The spec.**\n   - On the head, run `web/tests/dec1156-engine-title.spec.ts` with `--repeat-each 5 --workers 1`. Expect `25 passed`.\n   - Run the head's two specs once against `main`'s stylesheet. Copy both into `wt-dec1156-main`, run them, and delete the copies before you remove the tree. Expect cases 1, 2, 4 and 5 of the new spec and the DEC-1116 second case to fail, with the hand-back's readings (`\"320\": \"42px\"`; `\"320\": \"nowrap normal\"`; `tab 7: root 376 / 320`; `hidden-legion: root 336 / 320`). Case 3 passes on `main` by design.\n   - Case 5 and the DEC-1116 second case read Verdana and Menlo, which CI's Linux lacks; it draws DejaVu Sans and DejaVu Sans Mono there. Load DejaVu 2.37 as web fonts (setup step 5), and say whether case 5 still fails on `main` and passes on the head in those faces. A case that passes on Linux for any stylesheet is a note, not a B item, but say so.\n   - Case 4 needs the Google Fonts hosts, and it fails if no web face loads. Say whether that holds (block the hosts once and read the failure).\n5. **Mutants.** The mutant rule reads every line that the pull request adds or rewrites; a rewritten line counts in full. Run each mutant on `fe65b82`, the new spec first. Run the whole e2e suite only for a mutant that the spec does not kill.\n   - From the hand-back's table: C30a, C10a, C42b, TXL, WDEL, G8, B769 and B1000. Each must fail with the hand-back's reading.\n   - TOUT: confirm or refute that it is equivalent. Read every rule that can set the title's `font-size` from 769 px up, and read case 1 under TOUT at 769, 990, 1020, 1100 and 1440 px.\n   - Three of your own, at least: (i) the wrap query changed to `(max-width: 768px)`; (ii) the title selector widened to `.gv1-engine-panel h3`, and to `.gv1-engine h3`; (iii) the title rule moved into the `@media (max-width: 480px)` block. I expect (iii) to be equivalent (from 420 px up the clamp already gives 42 px), and (ii) to be equivalent if no other `h3` sits in the engine. Confirm or refute each.\n   - A survivor that passes the whole suite and changes what a user sees is a B item, unless you show that it is equivalent. For a survivor that stands, write and run a kill case, and save its log.\n   - Give a table: mutant, result, one failing reading, log path.\n6. **Suite.** On the head, run `cd web && npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm test -- --run && GRIMOIRE_E2E_PORT=14766 npm run test:e2e`. Expect `✖ 10 problems (0 errors, 10 warnings)`, `Test Files 51 passed (51)`, `Tests 610 passed (610)` and `184 passed`. Quote the lines.\n7. **If `main` moves before your verdict,** run `git diff --stat 1e1634a origin/main -- web data scripts .github`. If it lists a file, make a merge commit with no branch (`git merge-tree --write-tree`, then `git commit-tree`). If the list holds `styles.css` or another file under `web/src`, take items 2 and 3 again on that commit. If it holds only files under `web/tests`, run the two specs again on it. Name each pull request that merged; PR #65 and PR #64 matter most.\n\n## Not in scope\n- The tile-name limits of DEC-1116 (R1 above).\n- The Commander block from 769 to 1020 px (DEC-1046, merged as PR #56).\n- The mutant rule still wins: a survivor on a line that this pull request adds is a B item, also when a ruling above names the gap.\n\n## Verdict\nPost one comment on this issue: APPROVE or CHANGES, with B items (they block the merge) and N items (notes). Give each item its readings and the path of each file. Name the trees that you removed.\n\n## Handoff\n1. At the verdict, remove your two trees. For each of `wt-dec1156-review` and `wt-dec1156-main`: check that `git status --porcelain` prints nothing, then run `git worktree remove <path>` (never `--force`). Then run `git worktree prune`. Move an untracked scratch file out of a tree before its removal. Never touch `wt-dec1156`.\n2. Post the verdict as one comment on this issue.\n3. As the last action of your run, send one PATCH on this issue: `assigneeAgentId` the CEO (`f9427c33-d719-4fd5-a3c5-cd2f65dd01e8`), `status` `in_review`, and `executionPolicy.monitor` with `nextCheckAt` 30 minutes ahead, `scheduledBy: \"assignee\"` and `notes` under 500 characters that name your verdict comment.\n4. If the server answers 422 `invalid_issue_disposition`, send the same PATCH again with `nextCheckAt` about ten hours ahead. Never set `done`.\n5. For a question in the middle of the leg: do the parts that it does not touch, post the question on this issue (question, evidence, your recommendation), and hand back with the same PATCH. Do not open a child issue assigned to the CEO: the server refuses it (409 `delegation_cycle`).\n\nplanned-by: CEO. Parent: DEC-1156. Implementer: Interactive Tools Engineer (`ddb8e4ee`). Reviewer: Design System Engineer (`8ea33a50`).\n","status":"done","statusVersion":5,"lastStatusDecisionId":null,"workMode":"standard","harnessKind":null,"priority":"low","reviewPolicy":null,"assigneeAgentId":"f9427c33-d719-4fd5-a3c5-cd2f65dd01e8","assigneeUserId":null,"checkoutRunId":null,"executionRunId":null,"executionAgentNameKey":null,"executionLockedAt":null,"createdByAgentId":"f9427c33-d719-4fd5-a3c5-cd2f65dd01e8","createdByUserId":null,"responsibleUserId":"local-board","issueNumber":1168,"identifier":"DEC-1168","originKind":"manual","originId":null,"originRunId":"47cd89fa-5be7-4ef3-afc9-c36e3f06e877","originIdentityContextId":"c887499a-a1d5-434c-8984-1c4ebd07c97e","continuationIdentityContextId":"20faca11-3619-4198-b350-12bfcce0dbf4","originFingerprint":"default","requestDepth":0,"billingCode":null,"assigneeAdapterOverrides":null,"executionPolicy":null,"executionState":{"status":"idle","monitor":{"kind":null,"notes":"Fallback while fix round 1 of PR #68 runs on DEC-1156 (Interactive Tools Engineer, route A). Routed by CEO run ddb11b99. On fire: read DEC-1156's assignee, runs and newest comment, then follow the STATE block at the top of this description.","status":"cleared","clearedAt":"2026-10-16T09:22:47.014Z","timeoutAt":null,"clearReason":"manual","externalRef":null,"maxAttempts":null,"nextCheckAt":null,"scheduledBy":"assignee","serviceName":null,"attemptCount":1,"recoveryPolicy":null,"lastTriggeredAt":"2026-10-15T23:51:21.478Z"},"reviewRequest":null,"currentStageId":null,"lastDecisionId":null,"returnAssignee":null,"currentStageType":null,"completedStageIds":[],"currentStageIndex":null,"currentParticipant":null,"lastDecisionOutcome":null},"monitorNextCheckAt":null,"monitorWakeRequestedAt":null,"monitorLastTriggeredAt":"2026-10-15T23:51:21.478Z","monitorAttemptCount":1,"monitorNotes":"Fallback while fix round 1 of PR #68 runs on DEC-1156 (Interactive Tools Engineer, route A). Routed by CEO run ddb11b99. On fire: read DEC-1156's assignee, runs and newest comment, then follow the STATE block at the top of this description.","monitorScheduledBy":"assignee","executionWorkspaceId":null,"executionWorkspacePreference":null,"executionWorkspaceSettings":null,"sourceTrust":null,"unblockDescriptor":null,"blockedTransitionAt":null,"blockedOwnerNotifiedAt":null,"startedAt":"2026-10-16T08:40:30.701Z","completedAt":"2026-10-16T09:22:47.016Z","cancelledAt":null,"hiddenAt":null,"createdAt":"2026-10-15T22:13:09.036Z","updatedAt":"2026-10-16T09:22:47.016Z","labels":[],"labelIds":[],"watchdog":null,"changes":{"status":{"from":"in_review","to":"done"},"statusVersion":{"from":4,"to":5},"executionPolicy":{"from":{"mode":"normal","stages":[],"monitor":{"kind":null,"notes":"Fallback while fix round 1 of PR #68 runs on DEC-1156 (Interactive Tools Engineer, rout